framework_component_specs.PillarCard:
# PillarCard

Content hub navigation card with a 16:9 image, linked title, description, optional child articles, and footer CTA.

File: `app/articles/PillarCard.tsx`. Use within a React Router route tree. Navigation uses `Link` from `react-router`; no loader or action is required.

## Props

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `href` | `string` | Required | Pillar page URL |
| `title` | `string` | Required | Pillar title |
| `description` | `string` | Required | Pillar description |
| `heading` | `string` | — | Small heading above title |
| `image` | `string` | — | Pillar image URL |
| `imageAlt` | `string` | `title` | Image alt text |
| `fallbackImage` | `string` | — | Image used after loading failure |
| `childLinks` | `ChildLink[]` | — | Related articles |
| `maxChildren` | `number` | `3` | Maximum children shown |
| `ctaLabel` | `string` | `"View all"` | Footer text |
| `ctaHref` | `string` | `href` | Footer destination |
| `priority` | `boolean` | `false` | Eager, high-priority image loading |
| `className` | `string` | — | Additional card classes |

## Implementation

```tsx
import { Link } from "react-router";
import type { ReactElement } from "react";

type ChildLink = {
  title: string;
  href: string;
  description?: string;
};

type PillarCardProps = {
  href: string;
  title: string;
  description: string;
  heading?: string;
  image?: string;
  imageAlt?: string;
  fallbackImage?: string;
  childLinks?: ChildLink[];
  maxChildren?: number;
  ctaLabel?: string;
  ctaHref?: string;
  priority?: boolean;
  className?: string;
};

export default function PillarCard({
  href, title, description, heading, image, imageAlt = title,
  fallbackImage, childLinks = [], maxChildren = 3,
  ctaLabel = "View all", ctaHref = href, priority = false, className,
}: PillarCardProps): ReactElement {
  return (
    <article className={className}>
      {image && (
        <Link to={href}>
          <img
            key={image}
            src={image}
            alt={imageAlt}
            loading={priority ? "eager" : "lazy"}
            fetchPriority={priority ? "high" : "auto"}
            style={{ aspectRatio: "16 / 9", width: "100%", objectFit: "cover" }}
            onError={(event) => {
              const target = event.currentTarget;
              if (fallbackImage && !target.dataset.fallback) {
                target.dataset.fallback = "true";
                target.src = fallbackImage;
                return;
              }
              target.hidden = true;
            }}
          />
        </Link>
      )}
      <div>
        {heading && <span>{heading}</span>}
        <h3><Link to={href}>{title}</Link></h3>
        <p>{description}</p>
        {childLinks.length > 0 && maxChildren > 0 && (
          <ul>
            {childLinks.slice(0, maxChildren).map((child) => (
              <li key={child.href}>
                <span>{child.title}</span>
                {child.description && <p>{child.description}</p>}
                <Link to={child.href} aria-label={`View ${child.title}`}>View</Link>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        )}
      </div>
      <Link to={ctaHref}>{ctaLabel} <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></Link>
    </article>
  );
}
```

## Route JSX Example

```tsx
<PillarCard
  href="/pillars/ai"
  title="AI Fundamentals"
  description="Explore artificial intelligence."
  childLinks={[{ title: "Machine Learning", href: "/articles/ml" }]}
/>
```

## Presentation and Accessibility

Use a white, subtly bordered/shadowed, rounded card; rounded image top; bold title; muted description limited to 2–3 lines; compact children with right-aligned View links; full-width subtle footer; hover lift/shadow and visible keyboard focus. Match existing styling tokens without inventing a theme. Retain semantic `article`, descriptive image alt text, identifiable links, and an `h3` appropriate to the surrounding hierarchy.

## Semantic Hints

`pillar`, `category`, `topic-card`, `section-card`, `hub-card`, `collection-card`, `category-card`

