## Semantic Hints
`hero`, `header`, `banner`, `page-header`, `page-hero`, `headline`, `masthead`, `jumbotron`

## Structure
Outer `<div>` → labelled `<section>` → constrained content `<div>` → text `<div>` containing `<h1>`, optional `<p>`, and optional children wrapper.

## Variants and Styling
- `primary`: main pages; brand background.
- `secondary`: secondary pages; lighter brand background.
- `neutral`: minimal pages; gray or white background.
- Keep the wrapper full width and constrain inner content.
- Use a large, bold title, muted description, comfortable line height, generous vertical padding, and separation above children.
- Adapt title size and padding for mobile using established project styles.
- The example exposes semantic classes and `data-variant` for theme styling. Reuse project tokens; no color, radius, or breakpoint conventions are assumed.

## Accessibility
Use one page-level `<h1>`. Associate the section with its heading using `aria-labelledby`, creating a named region without declaring a second banner landmark. Maintain text contrast, visible focus indicators, and keyboard-accessible children.

## Complete React Router Example
`app/articles/HeroSection.tsx` exports the reusable component and a default route component. Register this module as the articles route in the project's React Router route configuration. It is SSR-safe; no `"use client"` directive is needed.

