```

## Styling and Accessibility
Rounded container, left accent border, bold heading and inline labels, and spaced semantic bullets. Indigo uses 50/500/900 colors; gray uses 50/400/900. Brand uses CSS variables with indigo fallbacks; no configured brand palette is assumed. Verify contrast for overrides. Keep the `h2` appropriate to the surrounding article hierarchy.

framework_component_specs.ArticleCalendarSection:
# ArticleCalendarSection

## Purpose
Interactive article archive calendar with month navigation, date filtering, and paginated results. Use on archive/calendar routes, not inside individual articles.

File: `app/articles/ArticleCalendarSection.tsx`. Use module-level type aliases and named function declarations. No `"use client";` is required unless this is a client-only integration module.

## Props
| Prop | Type | Default / description |
|---|---|---|
| `title` | `string` | Required section heading |
| `articles` | `Article[]` | Required complete calendar dataset |
| `paginatedArticles` | `Article[]` | Required visible results |
| `currentPage` | `number` | Required current page, starting at 1 |
| `totalPages` | `number` | Required page count |
| `pageSize` | `number` | Required articles per page |
| `paginationBasePath` | `string` | Required pagination URL base |
| `id` | `string` | `"calendar"`; section anchor ID |
| `paginationHash` | `string` | Optional URL fragment |
| `selectedDate` | `Date` | Optional selected date |
| `onDateSelect` | `(date: Date) => void` | Optional date-click callback |

```tsx
type Article = {
  slug: string;
  title: string;
  date: string;
  description?: string;
  image?: string;
};
```

`date` is an ISO date string. Use UTC calendar dates consistently, including date-only strings.

## Structure and behavior
- Render `<section id={id}>`, an `<h2>`, calendar, article cards, and pagination.
- Previous/next month buttons change the displayed month without navigating. Initialize from `selectedDate`, otherwise today.
- Use seven columns, Sunday–Saturday headers, and blank cells outside the month.
- Highlight dates containing articles, selected dates, and today distinctly. Clicking a day calls `onDateSelect`.
- Render `paginatedArticles` as article cards keyed by `slug`; article destinations and pagination use React Router `Link`.
- Pagination uses `page` query parameters. Preserve existing filters and append `paginationHash`; omit unavailable previous/next links.
- Keep filtering and pagination in the parent route. A date change resets page to 1.
- Use Tailwind utilities without prescribing unestablished tokens or breakpoints; allow narrow-screen calendar scrolling.

## Accessibility
Use `role="grid"` with rows and gridcells. Put `aria-selected` on gridcells and buttons inside them. Provide full-date accessible names, roving focus, arrow-key movement, and Enter/Space activation. Announce month changes through a polite live region. Label pagination `<nav aria-label="Article pagination">`; mark its current link with `aria-current="page"`.

## React Router route example
```tsx
import { useSearchParams } from "react-router";
import ArticleCalendarSection from "./ArticleCalendarSection";

const ARTICLES = [
  { slug: "launch", title: "Launch", date: "2024-01-15" },
];
const PAGE_SIZE = 9;

export default function ArchiveRoute() {
  const [params, setParams] = useSearchParams();
  const date = params.get("date");
  const selectedDate = date ? new Date(date) : undefined;
  const validDate = selectedDate &&
    !Number.isNaN(selectedDate.getTime()) ? selectedDate : undefined;
  const filtered = ARTICLES.filter((article) =>
    !validDate || article.date === validDate.toISOString().slice(0, 10)
  );
  const totalPages = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(filtered.length / PAGE_SIZE));
  const page = Math.min(totalPages,
    Math.max(1, Math.floor(Number(params.get("page"))) || 1));
  return (
    <ArticleCalendarSection
      title="Article Archive"
      articles={ARTICLES}
      paginatedArticles={filtered.slice((page - 1) * PAGE_SIZE, page * PAGE_SIZE)}
      currentPage={page}
      totalPages={totalPages}
      pageSize={PAGE_SIZE}
      paginationBasePath="/articles/archive"
      selectedDate={validDate}
      onDateSelect={(value: Date): void => {
        const next = new URLSearchParams(params);
        next.set("date", value.toISOString().slice(0, 10));
        next.set("page", "1");
        setParams(next);
      }}
    />
  );
}
```

## Semantic hints
`calendar`, `schedule`, `dates`, `events-calendar`, `date-picker`, `archive`, `timeline`

